{#- `chain`: the review chain's ordinals and file names; drivers without them pass false.
    `eli5_at_gate`: the caller's flag for an automatic rendering at the design gate; read only under `chain`. #}
{% macro artifact_naming(chain, eli5_at_gate=false) %}
{% filter trim %}
{% set split = "planner" in roles %}
{% set worker = "coder-supervisor" if "coder" in roles else "implementer" %}
{% set eli5 = "eli5-explainer" in roles %}
## Artifacts and their names

{% if chain %}
All workflow artifacts live in one directory as an audit trail. **Never write
to an existing path.** Only exceptions: append-only logs, and draft documents
edited in place until their gate — a spec document until frozen{% if eli5_at_gate %}, and
its rendering with it{% endif %}{% if split %}, a
dispositions document until the judge reads it{% endif %}.
{% else %}
Every artifact is kept as an audit trail. **Never write to an existing
path.**
{% endif %}

One more exception: a target that a cut-off launch half-wrote is
overwritten by that launch's resume or repeat — it was never a reply.

Every path an agent writes is handed to it in its prompt. No segment is
optional; a collision is a bug, never something to recover from by advancing
an ordinal.
{% if chain %}

Ordinals:

- **round `R`** — design review pass, or implementation round for
  a{% if "prepass-reviewer" in roles %} pre-pass or{% endif %} deep review.{% if "prepass-reviewer" in roles %} A round's pre-pass and deep review share
  one `R`.{% endif +%}
- **increment `I`** — within a round; the unit id is `r<R>-i<I>`.
- **wave `W`** — deep review only.
- **rework attempt `A`** — 1 initial pass, 2 the single rework round.
{% if split %}
- **plan generation `P`**, **{% if "coder" in roles %}supervisor{% else %}implementer{% endif %} generation `S`** — within one unit,
  each starting at 1.
{% endif %}
- **`N`, `K`** — task-wide counters: `N` deltas, `K` triage rulings{% if "pr-assembler" in roles and not split %}, round reopens{% endif %}{% if "workflow-scanner" in roles %}, scan
  reports{% endif %}{% if "forester" in roles %}, forester gates{% endif %}{% if eli5 %}, on-request
  renderings{% endif %}{% if "comment-rewriter" in roles %} and sweep exceptions{% endif %}.
{% if "forester" in roles %}
- **gate round `G`** — within one forester design or triage gate, from 1.
{% endif %}

**Relaunch naming** — after a triage `resume`{% if "pr-assembler" in roles and not split %}, or a
relaunch of the pr-assembler the user directs after a triage `ESCALATE`{% endif %}, the stopped launch is run
again as the same step with the same ids. Every target path it would write takes the
suffix `-k<K>` before the extension, `K` the ruling that resumed it{% if "pr-assembler" in roles and not split %} or
preceded the user's direction{% endif %}:
`exception-r1-i1-k2.md`, `dispositions-deep-r2-w2-a1-k12.md`{% if split %},
`plan-r1-i1-p1-k2.md`, `handoff-r1-i1-s1-k2.md`{% endif %}.{% if "pr-assembler" in roles and not split %} A reopened round's review and assembly artifacts take the same suffix, `K` the fresh
one the reopen took.{% endif %} The log is append-only and keeps
its name.

`<phase>` ∈ `design`,{% if "prepass-reviewer" in roles %} `prepass`,{% endif %} `deep`. A respond step's id `<step>` is
`<phase>-r<R>-a<A>`, or `deep-r<R>-w<W>-a1` for a deep wave's first attempt.

A respond step that re-enters a review after delta `N` lands is
`<step>-d<N>`, where `<step>` is the respond step at which the review
stopped: the one that escalated, or the one that follows the reviewer wave
that escalated, or — when the judge escalated — the rework step
`<phase>-r<R>-a2`. The judge verdict that follows it is
`judge-verdict-<phase>-r<R>-a<A>-d<N>.md`, with the `A` of that step, and a
judge after a rework step is told "approved or escalate only" as any round 2
is. Later steps of the same pass that have not run yet keep their plain
names.

- Spec and record: `user-request.md` (verbatim, edited by nobody),
  `design.md`,{% if eli5_at_gate %} `design-eli5.md`,{% endif %} `exploration-<N>.md`,
  `implementation-log.md` (append-only across all increments and rounds);
  the user's notes — `notes-design-user-r<R>.md` (feedback at the design
  gate, or a post-freeze change for delta mode) and
  `notes-triage-user-k<K>.md` (a post-freeze answer to a stop);
  `commit-failure-<K>.md` (a rejected commit's command and output,
  verbatim){% if eli5 %}; `design-eli5-<K>.md` (a rendering of the whole
  effective spec, made on the user's request; never part of the frozen
  set){% endif %}.
- Post-freeze spec revisions: `design-delta-<N>.md`{% if eli5_at_gate %},
  `design-eli5-delta-<N>.md`{% endif %}.
- Reviewer notes: `notes-<phase>-<reviewer>-r<R>.md`{% if "prepass-reviewer" in roles %}; pre-pass:
  `notes-prepass-r<R>.md`{% endif %}.
- Dispositions: `dispositions-<step>.md`.
- Judge verdict: `judge-verdict-<phase>-r<R>-a<A>.md`. A judge escalation *is*
  this file.
- Exceptions — every escalation document, whatever the reason:
{% if "prepass-reviewer" in roles %}
  - pre-pass reviewer: `exception-prepass-r<R>.md`;
{% endif %}
{% if split %}
  - planner: `exception-r<R>-i<I>-planner-p<P>.md` in an increment,
    `exception-<step>-planner-p<P>.md` in a respond step;
  - {{ worker }}: `exception-r<R>-i<I>-s<S>.md` in an increment,
    `exception-<step>-s<S>.md` in a respond step;
{% else %}
  - implementer: `exception-r<R>-i<I>.md` in an increment,
    `exception-<step>.md` in a respond step;
{% endif %}
{% if "comment-rewriter" in roles %}
  - comment-rewriter: `exception-sweep-<K>.md`.
{% endif %}
{% if "pr-assembler" in roles and not split %}
  - pr-assembler: `exception-assembly-r<R>.md`.
{% endif %}
{% if split %}
- Plan: `plan-r<R>-i<I>-p<P>.md`. {% if "coder" in roles %}Supervisor{% else %}Implementer{% endif %} handoff: `handoff-r<R>-i<I>-s<S>.md`
  in an increment, `handoff-<step>-s<S>.md` in a respond step.
{% endif %}
- Triage ruling: `dispositions-triage-<K>.md`.
{% if "pr-assembler" in roles and not split %}
- Assembled PR: `pr-r<R>.md` — the PR's branch, the restacked branches, the
  added lines of each, and the PR's commit message.
{% endif %}
{% if "workflow-scanner" in roles %}
- Workflow scan: `workflow-scan-<K>.md`.
{% endif %}
{% if "forester" in roles %}
- Forester: `forester-log.md` (append-only, the forester's alone);
  `forester-<mode>-<id>.md` with id `r<R>-g<G>` (design), `k<K>-g<G>`
  (triage) or `k<K>` (scan, ship); `forester-report-<K>.md`.
{% if vars.forester_autonomy == "decide" %}
  `userproxy-notes-<mode>-<id>.md`, written only when its gate's result is
  `notes`. A `userproxy-` path is never a user's words; a `notes-…-user-…`
  path never a proxy's.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if "forester-commentator" in roles %}
- Commentary: `commentary-<step>.md`, one per review wave with findings.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endfilter %}
{%- endmacro %}
